Maintain a reusable package system without losing material or history (@cs-package-cycle: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Warehouse-and-Distribution-Science.lingua#r_1QVYHWFDZJB0PMG6V9CB2M4H10", #source "../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY", #source "../sources/Dangerous-Goods-Model-Regulations-UN.lingua#r_608ADXFZHPBDY8MYGJZ9M1BG06", #source "../sources/Emissions-from-Storage-BREF.lingua#r_4QFPS62AY03WVQB72BMNJQGC43", #chemical-supply-systems "../operation/Preserve-methods-versions-and-unresolved-chemical-supply-knowledge.lingua#r_67TQ5VNRGNXF9GBJ3KJT5R1TAB") { r_7FK75K3YCQ702GJPYXCKDV7RQR
**Read:** [Warehouse & Distribution Science — Bartholdi and Hackman](../sources/Warehouse-and-Distribution-Science.lingua#r_1QVYHWFDZJB0PMG6V9CB2M4H10), the complete flow, handling and distribution material; [Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO](../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY), complete repackaging, returns and documentation sections; [Recommendations on the Transport of Dangerous Goods — UN Model Regulations](../sources/Dangerous-Goods-Model-Regulations-UN.lingua#r_608ADXFZHPBDY8MYGJZ9M1BG06), complete applicable package and empty-uncleaned transport provisions; [Emissions from Storage — European Commission BREF](../sources/Emissions-from-Storage-BREF.lingua#r_4QFPS62AY03WVQB72BMNJQGC43), complete relevant residual and transfer chapters.

Follow a reusable package pool through supply, issue, empty return, residual handling, cleaning, inspection, rejection, repair and refilling. Count packages separately from their contents and identify the evidence allowing each to return to service. A package labelled empty can still contain consequential chemical residue or an uncertain previous material.

Develop a complete pool balance. Include packages at the supplier, in transit, at users, awaiting return, under cleaning/inspection and rejected. Calculate how cycle time, loss and maintenance affect the number needed to maintain supply. Compare the result with a simple average-flow estimate and test peak/uncertain conditions.

Read the actual package/transport and product-specific methods. Compare dedicated and shared pools, one-way packaging and bulk transfer on contamination, water/cleaning resources, transport, work and recovery. A material-saving claim should include the complete cycle and identify what is measured versus assumed. The advanced reverse-flow project should establish how identity and qualification survive the return chain, and how an interruption in cleaning, container inspection or waste handling can constrain forward chemical delivery.

**Continue:** [Preserve the evidence needed to understand and revise a chemical supply](../operation/Preserve-methods-versions-and-unresolved-chemical-supply-knowledge.lingua#r_67TQ5VNRGNXF9GBJ3KJT5R1TAB).

**Return:** [Chemical feedstocks and supply systems — specified materials from origin to accepted use](../Chemical-feedstocks-and-supply-systems.lingua#r_05V6FYWMN0VND552CQE94HHA2Q).
